      <p><a href="/workbench/">Workbench</a></p>

      <h1>Field Notes</h1>

      <p>
        Field Notes are informal observations, implementation notes, and working
        notes related to Workbench usage and development.
      </p>

      <section aria-labelledby="purpose">
        <h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

        <p>
          Field Notes can document observations, design decisions, migration notes,
          and lessons from using the Workbench. They may cite Issues, Patterns,
          or Lenses, but they do not define canonical ontology entries.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="boundaries">
        <h2 id="boundaries">Boundaries</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Field Notes are not canonical Patterns.</li>
          <li>Field Notes are not canonical Lenses.</li>
          <li>Field Notes are not Issue source-of-truth pages.</li>
          <li>Field Notes are not receipts.</li>
          <li>Field Notes are not validation rules.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="planned">
        <h2 id="planned">Planned Note Types</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Implementation notes</li>
          <li>Design boundary notes</li>
          <li>Observed usage notes</li>
          <li>Migration notes</li>
          <li>Resolver and machine-output notes</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
